; A dependency version has to be three days old before this project installs it.
; Most malicious releases are pulled inside a day: the median takedown is 14
; hours, and three days stops about 94% of them. What it costs is three days
; between a real fix being published and this project being able to take it.
;
; npm 11 and later read this. npm 10 calls it an invalid option, and `npm config
; set` refuses to write it, which is why it is here by hand.
;
; `npm ci` is not affected either way. It installs what the lockfile already
; names, so this only applies when the tree is built: `npm install`, `npm update`.
min-release-age=3
